.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T17:00:21-08:00","id":1189724,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Chronicles_of_Darkness_books\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Wiki has lists of books.</a> They're not just a flat list and usually organized by date. I don't know if there's a second edition only one, outside of the obvious game lines like Demon and Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T02:14:58-08:00","id":1189808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1189468-book-list?p=1189720#post1189720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by &amp;quot;match interests&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the guys are interested in changeling, promethean, and gheist, but they want to know what the expansion books bring to the game, because they have to get ring-ins to make up numbers. The rest of us are going with the big three and hunter, and we just want to know what's available","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T05:12:00-08:00","id":1189831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1189468-book-list?p=1189808#post1189808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of the guys are interested in changeling, promethean, and gheist, but they want to know what the expansion books bring to the game, because they have to get ring-ins to make up numbers. The rest of us are going with the big three and hunter, and we just want to know what's available</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ring ins to make up numbers&quot;? What does that mean? Sorry for all the questions. Anyway,<br /> <br /> The expansion books for the base Chronicles of Darkness (known as the bluebook line colloquially), the expansion books for the big three or the expansions to those non-core splats the guys expressed interest in? Currently, I'm pretty sure there's only two bluebook expansions for 2e: The Hurt Locker (some new merits, minor and micro templates as well as extra rules on all sorts of violence) and Dark Eras (largely historical setting stuff with a few new systems and merits spread throughout, every era is a crossover between two templates or more).<br /> <br /> There is far more bluebook stuff for 1e though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}